Article 11 Under any of the following circumstances, the passport holder may apply for renewal or reissuance of a passport in accordance with the provisions:
(1) The validity period of the passport is about to expire;
(2) The visa pages of the passport are about to be used up;
(3) The passport is damaged and cannot be used;
(4) The passport is lost or stolen;
(5) Other circumstances where there is a legitimate reason for renewal or reissuance of the passport.
Where a passport holder applies for renewal or reissuance of an ordinary passport, if he or she is within the country, the application shall be made in person to the exit and entry administration department of the public security organ of the local people's government at or above the county level in the place of his or her registered residence; if he or she is abroad, the application shall be made in person to the embassy or consulate of the People's Republic of China abroad or to another overseas agency authorized by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Where a Chinese citizen residing abroad returns to China and applies for renewal or reissuance of an ordinary passport, the application shall be made in person to the exit and entry administration department of the public security organ of the local people's government at or above the county level in the place of his or her temporary residence.
The renewal or reissuance of diplomatic passports and service passports shall be handled in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

Article 13 The passport issuing authority shall not issue a passport to an applicant under any of the following circumstances:
(1) He or she does not have the nationality of the People's Republic of China;
(2) He or she cannot prove his or her identity;
(3) He or she practices fraud in the application process;
(4) He or she is serving a sentence imposed by a criminal judgment;
(5) A People's Court notifies that there is an unresolved civil case and he or she may not leave the country;
(6) He or she is a defendant in a criminal case or a criminal suspect;
(7) The relevant competent department of the State Council considers that the exit will cause harm to national security or cause significant losses to national interests.

Article 14 The passport issuing authority shall not issue a passport to an applicant under any of the following circumstances within a period ranging from six months to three years from the date of completion of the execution of the criminal punishment or the date of repatriation:
(1) He or she has been subjected to criminal punishment for obstructing the administration of national (border) boundaries;
(2) He or she has been repatriated for illegal exit, illegal stay or illegal employment.

Article 20 Any staff member of a passport issuing authority who commits any of the following acts in the process of handling passports shall be given an administrative sanction according to law; if the act constitutes a crime, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Failing to accept an application that should be accepted;
(2) Failing to issue a passport within the statutory time limit without legitimate reasons;
(3) Charging fees exceeding the standards prescribed by the State;
(4) Soliciting or accepting bribes from an applicant;
(5) Disclosing citizens' personal information learned during the production or issuance of passports, infringing upon the lawful rights and interests of citizens;
(6) Other acts of abusing power, neglecting duties, or engaging in malpractices for personal gain.
